# Do block 0's gates on the goal token make the goal-specific coordinates?

Generated by `gate0.py` (exploratory). At block 0 each head's attention mass on the goal token is replaced by its mean for that goal and query position (fit episodes, every goal), the other tokens' weights rescaled to keep their relative weights; goal content is kept, its history-dependent gating removed. 'Simplified' = section 14's network with all four MLPs replaced by shared affine maps at every token. At the decision token under every goal (6144 test decisions): the variance shares of the goal part M(g) and of the goal × history interaction I(h, g) at the input of block 1 (site 1), of block 2 (site 2) and at the end (site 4); R² of the state from a shared MLP encoder of the posterior plus a goal offset against per-goal encoders (the gap is the goal-specific coding of the belief); on the A-equivalent, B-different pairs, R² of the untransformed A-written difference Δ_A for the B-written Δ_B and of the fitted map's M(A→B) Δ_A (ridge on 12 288 fit pairs); the transport test at the input of block 2 (B's decision switched to the donor's by Δ_B, by M(A→B) Δ_A, by Δ_A, by random). Behaviour: recovery of the goal-directed return over the goal-blind floor; agreement with the natural model's own-goal decisions (all / goal-dependent). Medians (min–max) over six models.

## The gates

Mass on the goal token at decision tokens after the first step: 0.23 (0.22–0.28); per goal 0.27 (0.22–0.35), 0.21 (0.19–0.25), 0.21 (0.19–0.26), 0.25 (0.22–0.32); per head 0.26 (0.16–0.46), 0.28 (0.17–0.32), 0.19 (0.18–0.25), 0.22 (0.17–0.34).
Its spread across histories within one (goal, head, step): std 0.10 (0.08–0.12); the std of the means across goals 0.08 (0.06–0.08).

## Behaviour and the interaction

The state as hist(h) + M(g) + I(h, g) (section 6's decomposition) and, with the goal offset allowed to depend on the step, as hist(h) + M(g, step) + I'(h, g): the share of the goal × step offset and of the interaction beyond it.

